1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,880
Why do I feel like
I don't suspect Amp at all?

2
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:02,930
Get a grip, Podduang.

3
00:00:02,950 --> 00:00:04,310
A hater is a hater.

4
00:00:04,330 --> 00:00:04,940
[Don't get involved in Anda's case
if you still wanna live.]

5
00:00:04,970 --> 00:00:06,320
Do you think it's Amp?

6
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:08,070
Why would she do something like that?

7
00:00:08,210 --> 00:00:10,790
She knows we're investigating this, that's why.

8
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:12,190
Anda said...

9
00:00:12,210 --> 00:00:14,040
if the day came when he had to go,

10
00:00:14,070 --> 00:00:15,560
he wanted Dad and Mom...
[If my mom knows that I like this friend,]

11
00:00:15,590 --> 00:00:17,110
to bring the box to the cremation as well.
[will she be happy...?]

12
00:00:19,130 --> 00:00:21,730
I'll return and take over your business.

13
00:00:21,850 --> 00:00:25,130
You have to let me see
every CCTV in your condo.

14
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:27,230
Amp is James's girlfriend...

15
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:28,460
Jealousy is clearly the motive.

16
00:00:28,490 --> 00:00:30,410
They've fought over this many times.

17
00:00:30,430 --> 00:00:32,870
And do you know where James is now?

18
00:00:33,860 --> 00:00:35,240
I really do promise.

19
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:37,500
I'll definitely get the money.

20
00:00:38,350 --> 00:00:39,360
A million, okay?

21
00:00:39,690 --> 00:00:40,420
Boss.

22
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:41,730
He's asking for another million.

23
00:00:42,150 --> 00:00:44,000
I've found someone
with even worse luck than you.

24
00:00:51,150 --> 00:00:51,770
No...

25
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:00,550
Please...

26
00:01:08,680 --> 00:01:10,800
Don't do anything to me. I'm begging.

27
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:11,690
No!

28
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:12,420
Please!

29
00:01:22,350 --> 00:01:23,490
What's next, Boss?

30
00:01:24,380 --> 00:01:25,550
You can take a break for now.

31
00:01:28,490 --> 00:01:29,750
Let this guy take over.

32
00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:32,650
Go on.

33
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:43,440
Go!

34
00:02:09,039 --> 00:02:11,460
[The depicted characters, behaviors, locations,
organizations, professions, and events]

35
00:02:11,490 --> 00:02:13,590
[are fictional and created
for entertainment purposes only.]

36
00:02:13,620 --> 00:02:15,800
[It is not intended to endorse or promote
any of the actions or behavior depicted.]

37
00:02:15,830 --> 00:02:17,140
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

38
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:35,820
♫I used to wonder what we were,♫

39
00:02:35,850 --> 00:02:41,810
♫I thought love needed something clearer,♫

40
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:47,829
♫Took me time to learn what really matters♫

41
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:54,530
♫Love has no rules, whatever comes after♫

42
00:02:55,940 --> 00:03:01,420
♫As long as I know what my heart wants to find,♫

43
00:03:01,710 --> 00:03:04,240
♫As long as you're standing by my side,♫

44
00:03:04,270 --> 00:03:07,530
♫With you, the only one I'd choose every time,♫

45
00:03:07,550 --> 00:03:11,380
♫I don't need a reason, as long as you're mine♫

46
00:03:11,990 --> 00:03:14,550
♫As long as you hold my hand,♫

47
00:03:15,060 --> 00:03:17,550
♫As long as next to me is where you stand,♫

48
00:03:17,570 --> 00:03:20,860
♫You're the one I'll always try to understand,♫

49
00:03:20,890 --> 00:03:24,710
♫No matter how hard the road may be,♫

50
00:03:25,360 --> 00:03:28,030
♫Just hold my hand, and we'll be free♫

51
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:31,360
♫As long as you're here with me♫

52
00:03:48,430 --> 00:03:49,590
What's wrong?

53
00:03:52,240 --> 00:03:53,070
Nothing, sir.

54
00:03:57,410 --> 00:03:58,420
Are you scared?

55
00:04:01,170 --> 00:04:02,530
Don't be.

56
00:04:03,170 --> 00:04:04,340
That security guard

57
00:04:05,020 --> 00:04:06,520
only asked me for one million.

58
00:04:07,300 --> 00:04:09,430
If you can't come up
with two million to pay me back,

59
00:04:09,970 --> 00:04:11,950
I'll make sure
you get the premium treatment.

60
00:04:11,970 --> 00:04:13,390
Please don't kill me, sir.

61
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:15,990
Please don't kill me.

62
00:04:16,019 --> 00:04:16,940
Hey.

63
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:19,160
Why would I kill you?

64
00:04:19,750 --> 00:04:21,459
You're so useful.

65
00:04:22,180 --> 00:04:23,790
I'll definitely keep you around.

66
00:04:25,520 --> 00:04:27,220
I'll get you the money as fast as I can.

67
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:29,480
No.

68
00:04:29,840 --> 00:04:31,240
You don't need to.

69
00:04:35,230 --> 00:04:37,610
Do you want your debt to be wiped out?

70
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:57,460
What do you want me to do, sir?

71
00:04:59,640 --> 00:05:01,220
You're quite a quick learner.

72
00:05:02,210 --> 00:05:03,710
I'm ready, sir.

73
00:05:03,730 --> 00:05:05,210
I'm ready to do anything.

74
00:05:05,880 --> 00:05:07,790
I heard you and my brother

75
00:05:08,340 --> 00:05:09,940
acted together in those shows.

76
00:05:11,550 --> 00:05:12,240
Yes, sir.

77
00:05:13,340 --> 00:05:15,410
But I didn't realize that your girlfriend...

78
00:05:20,290 --> 00:05:21,810
was one of my brother's haters.

79
00:05:26,880 --> 00:05:27,830
Well?

80
00:05:31,370 --> 00:05:32,840
Now, why don't you guess

81
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:35,450
what I want you to do next?

82
00:05:37,230 --> 00:05:38,950
Sir... Sir.

83
00:05:43,450 --> 00:05:45,490
Hey.

84
00:05:46,300 --> 00:05:47,920
There's no need to kill anyone.

85
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:51,020
I'm not that cold-hearted.

86
00:05:52,550 --> 00:05:54,750
But do you know your girlfriend

87
00:05:55,400 --> 00:05:58,170
is the prime suspect
in my brother's case right now?

88
00:06:01,310 --> 00:06:02,720
I know about that, sir.

89
00:06:02,750 --> 00:06:05,080
But I really don't know
if she killed Anda or not.

90
00:06:05,110 --> 00:06:06,310
I truly swear.

91
00:06:06,340 --> 00:06:07,480
I really don't know.

92
00:06:07,510 --> 00:06:09,010
I haven't been in touch with her.

93
00:06:09,400 --> 00:06:11,650
I don't know where she is, sir.

94
00:06:12,270 --> 00:06:13,680
Stop talking.

95
00:06:14,400 --> 00:06:15,460
It's annoying.

96
00:06:23,870 --> 00:06:27,090
I just want to know where she is right now.

97
00:06:27,510 --> 00:06:29,090
And can you get ahold of her?

98
00:06:30,210 --> 00:06:33,620
Lately, I've been fighting
with her about money.

99
00:06:34,210 --> 00:06:35,310
And then she just disappeared.

100
00:06:35,330 --> 00:06:36,610
I tried calling her,
but she didn't answer.

101
00:06:37,020 --> 00:06:38,420
Then do you have any idea

102
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:39,750
where she might be?

103
00:06:40,490 --> 00:06:41,930
I don't know.

104
00:06:46,260 --> 00:06:47,990
You're becoming useless to me.

105
00:06:48,460 --> 00:06:49,270
Sir!

106
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:50,550
Sir.

107
00:06:51,350 --> 00:06:52,890
I'll track her down
for you as soon as I can.

108
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:54,350
I'll find her, sir.

109
00:06:54,370 --> 00:06:55,190
I promise.

110
00:06:55,220 --> 00:06:56,780
I'll find her.

111
00:06:58,900 --> 00:06:59,770
Yeah.

112
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:11,420
Bring your girlfriend to me,

113
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,410
and your debt will be wiped out.

114
00:07:15,490 --> 00:07:16,240
Sir.

115
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:18,680
What are you going to do to her?

116
00:07:18,710 --> 00:07:20,240
She's pregnant right now.

117
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:26,680
What would a "good" cop like me

118
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:28,670
do to a pregnant woman?

119
00:07:33,790 --> 00:07:35,210
The one who's going to do it...

120
00:07:36,140 --> 00:07:37,370
is you.

121
00:07:52,870 --> 00:07:53,710
[Who killed Anda?]

122
00:07:58,120 --> 00:07:59,880
Are you two Sherlock Holmes?

123
00:08:00,130 --> 00:08:02,130
I've got Conan in my room,
and I thought that was a lot.

124
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:03,890
Now I have to deal with Watson

125
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:04,850
and Sherlock.

126
00:08:04,870 --> 00:08:06,210
I'm totally lost now.

127
00:08:08,610 --> 00:08:10,140
What did you two find?

128
00:08:11,270 --> 00:08:15,260
Regarding the CAN bus system
we talked about the other day,

129
00:08:15,460 --> 00:08:17,210
Art and I tried it out ourselves.

130
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:18,490
The professor helped us with it,

131
00:08:18,510 --> 00:08:20,240
using the same car model as Anda's.
[Anda's car - A modification shop?]

132
00:08:20,380 --> 00:08:23,150
That same model isn't even hard to hack.

133
00:08:23,180 --> 00:08:24,300
That means...

134
00:08:24,640 --> 00:08:26,050
we can be 100% certain now, right?

135
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:28,080
That the car was hacked.

136
00:08:28,470 --> 00:08:29,220
Yes.

137
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:31,440
Because the professor who helped us

138
00:08:31,550 --> 00:08:34,570
is the same person the police
asked to check Anda's car.

139
00:08:35,140 --> 00:08:36,120
Which means...

140
00:08:37,169 --> 00:08:38,640
Anda's killer

141
00:08:39,010 --> 00:08:41,190
didn't even need to be
at the crime scene, right?

142
00:08:41,299 --> 00:08:41,940
Exactly.

143
00:08:42,490 --> 00:08:45,160
And are there no range limitations at all?

144
00:08:45,250 --> 00:08:46,400
There are three types.

145
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:48,010
Near, mid, and far.

146
00:08:48,040 --> 00:08:49,150
Far means unlimited.

147
00:08:49,180 --> 00:08:50,800
It can be done
from across the world via the internet.

148
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:54,380
That makes it really hard to know who it is.

149
00:08:56,020 --> 00:08:58,310
Yeah, we really don't have enough info.

150
00:09:01,570 --> 00:09:02,650
Not enough.

151
00:09:02,980 --> 00:09:04,720
But it's not a waste.

152
00:09:07,190 --> 00:09:09,110
Stop posing.

153
00:09:09,140 --> 00:09:10,520
Just say what you know already.

154
00:09:11,220 --> 00:09:14,020
There are many auto repair shops in Bangkok.

155
00:09:14,290 --> 00:09:17,370
But only a few can set up smart car systems

156
00:09:17,590 --> 00:09:19,240
on luxury cars like Anda's.

157
00:09:21,370 --> 00:09:22,740
What do you mean, Tod?

158
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:25,400
You're going to investigate
the auto repair shops, right?

159
00:09:26,180 --> 00:09:26,910
Yes.

160
00:09:27,580 --> 00:09:28,520
That won't be hard.

161
00:09:28,590 --> 00:09:31,210
I'll ask Itti
where Anda took his car to get repaired.

162
00:09:32,570 --> 00:09:35,850
If Anda's killer is linked to the car,

163
00:09:36,020 --> 00:09:37,250
then Amp seems unlikely, doesn't she?
[Amp - Anda hater]

164
00:09:37,270 --> 00:09:37,730
[Amp - James]

165
00:09:37,760 --> 00:09:38,210
[James - James's car]

166
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:39,980
From what I've gathered,
[Not a suicide]

167
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:41,880
Amp has nothing to do with cars,

168
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:44,150
other than paying for
James's car installments.

169
00:09:44,890 --> 00:09:46,790
But we can't be entirely sure yet, can we?

170
00:09:46,810 --> 00:09:48,290
Amp is such a real piece of work.

171
00:09:48,320 --> 00:09:50,290
She's ruthless
when it comes to being a hater.

172
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:52,860
She might have used those skills
to do something under Anda's car.

173
00:09:52,890 --> 00:09:53,680
Who knows?

174
00:09:53,980 --> 00:09:55,680
You've watched too many movies.

175
00:09:55,700 --> 00:09:56,540
Stop it.

176
00:09:56,570 --> 00:09:58,680
Anything is possible right now.

177
00:09:59,010 --> 00:10:00,450
Look at us. We're students,

178
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:01,930
yet here we are doing God knows what.

179
00:10:04,260 --> 00:10:06,290
We've come this far.

180
00:10:07,540 --> 00:10:08,770
Let's end this matter.

181
00:10:11,970 --> 00:10:12,660
[Amp's teddy]

182
00:10:12,680 --> 00:10:13,280
[Kum - Anda's boyfriend]

183
00:10:13,310 --> 00:10:13,800
[The security guard - "Thief"]

184
00:10:15,390 --> 00:10:17,190
We don't want to ruin the moment,

185
00:10:17,610 --> 00:10:19,830
but Jin, I thought we were here for drinks.

186
00:10:20,150 --> 00:10:22,280
Look, we've been working
on this board all day.

187
00:10:22,300 --> 00:10:23,790
We get tired too, you know.

188
00:10:24,420 --> 00:10:25,690
So Jin got you two...

189
00:10:26,120 --> 00:10:28,620
to come here for drinks?

190
00:10:28,820 --> 00:10:29,710
Exactly.

191
00:10:32,770 --> 00:10:33,700
Podduang.

192
00:10:35,210 --> 00:10:36,260
That means...

193
00:10:37,410 --> 00:10:39,030
you tricked us into coming here, too?

194
00:10:40,290 --> 00:10:43,290
Come on, we don't meet up often.

195
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:46,300
If I hadn't done this,
the case wouldn't have progressed.

196
00:10:46,800 --> 00:10:48,710
And we wouldn't have gotten together.

197
00:10:48,730 --> 00:10:49,790
Who said I tricked you?

198
00:10:56,340 --> 00:10:59,530
- Whoa.
- Whoa.

199
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:01,770
To our friendship!

200
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:03,960
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

201
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:06,600
- Bottoms up!
- Not me.

202
00:11:06,760 --> 00:11:07,860
Whoever's last has to go for another round.

203
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:08,700
That's me.

204
00:11:10,780 --> 00:11:13,220
Hey, everyone, we're out of ice.

205
00:11:16,040 --> 00:11:18,760
Let's spin the bottle to decide

206
00:11:18,990 --> 00:11:20,550
who goes to buy more ice.

207
00:11:20,580 --> 00:11:22,480
Here, I'll spin it.

208
00:11:26,870 --> 00:11:28,190
It's you, Dunk.

209
00:11:28,700 --> 00:11:29,800
Oh, come on!

210
00:11:30,360 --> 00:11:31,920
Come on, come on.

211
00:11:32,060 --> 00:11:32,930
This time...

212
00:11:33,280 --> 00:11:34,180
Whose money are we going to spend?

213
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:35,080
I'll do it.

214
00:11:35,310 --> 00:11:36,100
Help me, my boy.

215
00:11:38,300 --> 00:11:39,070
Watch this.

216
00:11:43,380 --> 00:11:44,180
Oops!

217
00:11:44,740 --> 00:11:45,840
It's Jin.

218
00:11:46,950 --> 00:11:48,030
I'll give it to you.

219
00:11:50,190 --> 00:11:51,380
Fine, I'll go with Dunk.

220
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:55,900
Hurry back,

221
00:11:56,740 --> 00:12:00,780
or Bumm and I might have to drink it all neat.

222
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:02,850
You're really something, aren't you?

223
00:12:02,930 --> 00:12:05,500
Ooh, look at you two lovebirds.

224
00:12:05,770 --> 00:12:08,450
Jin is so slick.

225
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:11,180
I'm going to make both of you go buy it.

226
00:12:11,310 --> 00:12:11,910
Go!

227
00:12:15,470 --> 00:12:16,770
Will you be able to practice tomorrow?

228
00:12:17,230 --> 00:12:18,470
I'm fine.

229
00:12:18,730 --> 00:12:19,470
What's there to be afraid of?

230
00:12:19,500 --> 00:12:20,980
I'm fine. What about you?

231
00:12:21,100 --> 00:12:22,370
Heck yeah, I am.

232
00:12:22,390 --> 00:12:23,740
I'm the host here.

233
00:12:24,980 --> 00:12:25,560
Is that so?

234
00:12:25,590 --> 00:12:26,720
Yeah.

235
00:12:27,280 --> 00:12:29,600
So, are you two actually dating?

236
00:12:29,910 --> 00:12:31,300
We've been dating for a long time.

237
00:12:31,680 --> 00:12:33,190
I mean, dating for real.

238
00:12:33,510 --> 00:12:34,490
Like, seriously.

239
00:12:34,860 --> 00:12:37,470
Not just pretending to fool others.

240
00:12:41,460 --> 00:12:42,470
You knew?

241
00:12:42,820 --> 00:12:43,750
Of course.

242
00:12:43,870 --> 00:12:45,350
Podduang is my best friend, you know.

243
00:12:45,420 --> 00:12:46,440
How could I not know?

244
00:12:48,540 --> 00:12:49,620
But do you know...

245
00:12:50,130 --> 00:12:51,360
that he actually likes you?

246
00:12:52,820 --> 00:12:53,760
He used to like me.

247
00:12:54,050 --> 00:12:55,550
Now Podduang doesn't like me anymore.

248
00:12:56,090 --> 00:12:58,300
I can tell just by
the way he looks at you, Jin.

249
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:00,400
What's with you?

250
00:13:00,840 --> 00:13:02,180
Talking like you're going to
take your friend back.

251
00:13:02,200 --> 00:13:03,440
I wouldn't do that.

252
00:13:03,710 --> 00:13:05,860
I'm actually glad that he likes you.

253
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:09,200
Why's that?

254
00:13:10,190 --> 00:13:12,200
You two are so easy to read.

255
00:13:13,260 --> 00:13:14,800
You've liked him for a long time,
haven't you?

256
00:13:15,580 --> 00:13:17,100
Take good care of him, then.

257
00:13:17,490 --> 00:13:18,770
And remember this, too.

258
00:13:18,790 --> 00:13:20,260
If you ever make him sad,

259
00:13:20,430 --> 00:13:21,710
I won't go easy on you, Jin.

260
00:13:22,610 --> 00:13:23,500
Are you threatening me?

261
00:13:23,750 --> 00:13:24,930
You could call it that.

262
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:27,070
So try to be a little scared of me.

263
00:13:27,380 --> 00:13:30,690
Bumm and I love Podduang
just as much as you do.

264
00:13:31,120 --> 00:13:31,770
Got it?

265
00:13:32,090 --> 00:13:34,110
Yeah, I understand.

266
00:13:34,930 --> 00:13:35,700
Let's go.

267
00:13:35,720 --> 00:13:37,120
The ice is melting all over my feet.

268
00:13:37,460 --> 00:13:38,090
Go.

269
00:13:44,270 --> 00:13:45,320
Give it here.

270
00:13:45,350 --> 00:13:47,250
You sound like a dying cat.

271
00:13:47,810 --> 00:13:49,410
Let me sing, too.

272
00:13:49,770 --> 00:13:52,290
No way. You're a terrible singer.

273
00:13:59,110 --> 00:14:00,870
Do you usually drink this much?

274
00:14:01,810 --> 00:14:02,960
You saw it yourself, didn't you?

275
00:14:03,150 --> 00:14:04,160
It was my birthday.

276
00:14:06,400 --> 00:14:08,380
Oh, right. That's true.

277
00:14:08,630 --> 00:14:10,530
But I didn't think
you'd get that hammered.

278
00:14:15,690 --> 00:14:16,390
Here.

279
00:14:16,980 --> 00:14:18,040
I'll give you another can.

280
00:14:18,870 --> 00:14:20,060
Or do you want two?

281
00:14:21,240 --> 00:14:22,530
You're so nice, huh?

282
00:14:26,750 --> 00:14:29,330
He's trying to get you drunk, Podduang.

283
00:14:31,890 --> 00:14:33,200
Really.

284
00:14:38,420 --> 00:14:39,280
Really?

285
00:14:40,340 --> 00:14:41,440
No.

286
00:14:42,070 --> 00:14:44,610
I just saw that you were happy.

287
00:14:45,440 --> 00:14:47,200
We've been through a lot.

288
00:14:47,630 --> 00:14:48,900
It's good to relax sometimes.

289
00:14:51,590 --> 00:14:52,390
Then...

290
00:14:53,590 --> 00:14:54,570
How about you have a drink with me?

291
00:14:55,960 --> 00:14:56,750
Sure thing.

292
00:15:04,550 --> 00:15:06,270
At this rate, they'll be at it all night.

293
00:15:18,970 --> 00:15:21,240
Wait, Podduang, calm down.

294
00:15:24,250 --> 00:15:25,200
Enough talking.

295
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:26,520
Podduang.

296
00:15:30,290 --> 00:15:31,490
Podduang.

297
00:15:31,530 --> 00:15:32,690
People will hear us.

298
00:15:33,740 --> 00:15:35,110
Not yet. The door isn't locked.

299
00:15:35,600 --> 00:15:38,680
- They're already asleep. Don't worry.
- Podduang, Podduang.

300
00:15:39,020 --> 00:15:41,070
Calm down. Easy, okay?

301
00:15:41,330 --> 00:15:43,780
Calm down, slow down.

302
00:15:44,950 --> 00:15:45,740
I'm hot.

303
00:15:46,840 --> 00:15:48,270
Calm down first.

304
00:15:48,310 --> 00:15:49,710
Our friends are all outside.

305
00:15:49,880 --> 00:15:53,320
They're all asleep.
What are you afraid of?

306
00:15:53,460 --> 00:15:54,300
Podduang.

307
00:15:58,620 --> 00:15:59,860
Stop.

308
00:15:59,890 --> 00:16:02,780
- I'm hot.
- Podduang, please.

309
00:16:02,810 --> 00:16:04,100
The others will hear.

310
00:16:05,180 --> 00:16:07,570
Can you take my shirt off for me?

311
00:16:08,040 --> 00:16:08,620
Podduang.

312
00:16:08,650 --> 00:16:11,350
- Take my shirt off.
- You're too drunk.

313
00:16:11,660 --> 00:16:12,900
Podduang, Podduang, Podduang.

314
00:16:15,370 --> 00:16:16,990
You're so drunk.

315
00:17:04,109 --> 00:17:05,640
Jin, I can't wait any longer.

316
00:19:20,720 --> 00:19:23,120
What the hell is this?

317
00:19:34,910 --> 00:19:36,380
Hello, Bumm.

318
00:19:36,560 --> 00:19:37,780
Hello.

319
00:19:38,260 --> 00:19:39,750
Where are you, Bumm?

320
00:19:40,500 --> 00:19:41,790
In my room.

321
00:19:42,810 --> 00:19:45,200
When did you guys leave?
You didn't even tell me.

322
00:19:45,230 --> 00:19:47,490
You don't remember a thing, do you?

323
00:19:48,650 --> 00:19:50,770
That's it. I'm going back to sleep.

324
00:19:50,980 --> 00:19:52,980
Wait, what?

325
00:20:02,790 --> 00:20:04,540
How did they even get in here?

326
00:20:10,790 --> 00:20:11,830
Jin.

327
00:20:12,610 --> 00:20:14,940
Let's shower together.
Take my shirt off.

328
00:20:14,970 --> 00:20:15,900
Podduang, Podduang.

329
00:20:16,370 --> 00:20:17,210
Take my shirt off.

330
00:20:17,230 --> 00:20:19,440
Can you take my shirt off?

331
00:20:23,550 --> 00:20:25,850
- Jin.
- My friend's quite a flirt, isn't he?

332
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:28,600
It's hot. So hot.

333
00:20:28,620 --> 00:20:30,070
I think I'd better head back.

334
00:20:30,520 --> 00:20:32,680
I forgot to do laundry. See ya.

335
00:20:32,710 --> 00:20:34,310
- Yeah, right.
- Jin.

336
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:35,850
Wait for me!

337
00:20:40,050 --> 00:20:41,710
Come on. Let's head back.

338
00:20:42,810 --> 00:20:44,130
Let's go. Get back to our room.

339
00:20:51,010 --> 00:20:52,090
Let's shower together.

340
00:20:59,860 --> 00:21:02,230
What the hell have I done?

341
00:21:19,880 --> 00:21:21,200
How many rounds was that last night?

342
00:21:24,360 --> 00:21:26,720
What messy eaters.

343
00:21:32,100 --> 00:21:33,020
Have a seat.

344
00:21:34,010 --> 00:21:35,000
I'll drive you back.

345
00:21:36,910 --> 00:21:39,060
It's okay. I can go back by myself.

346
00:21:39,080 --> 00:21:41,110
Hey, it's fine.

347
00:21:42,430 --> 00:21:43,420
I can drive you.

348
00:21:44,780 --> 00:21:46,950
It's quite surprising that

349
00:21:47,120 --> 00:21:48,430
Tycoon Chanin,

350
00:21:48,460 --> 00:21:51,180
the owner of one of
the country's leading real estate businesses,

351
00:21:51,200 --> 00:21:52,690
is stepping down from his position,

352
00:21:52,720 --> 00:21:54,980
with the son of his second wife

353
00:21:55,010 --> 00:21:56,600
taking over instead.

354
00:22:00,100 --> 00:22:02,670
You... made up with your dad, right?

355
00:22:04,120 --> 00:22:04,760
Yeah.

356
00:22:05,640 --> 00:22:06,810
Even though it's against my will.

357
00:22:07,140 --> 00:22:09,040
Why?

358
00:22:11,730 --> 00:22:13,430
I asked him to agree to two conditions:

359
00:22:16,160 --> 00:22:18,150
that I could see all the CCTV footage

360
00:22:19,500 --> 00:22:20,990
and that he would make sure you're safe.

361
00:22:29,490 --> 00:22:31,050
Ever since what happened to Anda,

362
00:22:32,150 --> 00:22:34,080
your life has been in constant danger.

363
00:22:35,240 --> 00:22:37,100
I don't want anything
to happen to you, Podduang.

364
00:22:39,720 --> 00:22:40,740
Thanks.

365
00:22:42,770 --> 00:22:46,050
But what do you mean by
asking your dad about me?

366
00:22:50,810 --> 00:22:54,440
♫Thank you for coming into my life♫

367
00:22:54,460 --> 00:22:58,920
♫Thank you for making this love feel right♫

368
00:22:59,020 --> 00:23:01,820
♫My heart is filled with bliss♫

369
00:23:01,840 --> 00:23:06,960
♫When we're holding hands like this♫

370
00:23:12,890 --> 00:23:14,420
My dad gave me a car to drive,

371
00:23:14,600 --> 00:23:16,700
but I think this way is better.

372
00:23:17,450 --> 00:23:18,900
What do you mean?

373
00:23:21,760 --> 00:23:23,470
Being able to stay close like this,

374
00:23:23,860 --> 00:23:24,920
isn't it better?

375
00:23:26,840 --> 00:23:27,640
Hey.

376
00:23:30,930 --> 00:23:32,590
But isn't this a bit too much?

377
00:23:35,780 --> 00:23:37,460
I understand.

378
00:23:37,930 --> 00:23:39,520
But it's because of the threat you got.

379
00:23:39,830 --> 00:23:40,560
That's the thing

380
00:23:40,770 --> 00:23:41,760
that really is a bit too much for me.

381
00:23:45,310 --> 00:23:46,390
Are you worried about me?

382
00:23:47,680 --> 00:23:48,520
Yeah.

383
00:23:50,620 --> 00:23:51,510
And...

384
00:23:53,770 --> 00:23:55,810
How closely do they have to follow us?

385
00:23:57,020 --> 00:23:59,050
I won't make you feel uncomfortable.

386
00:23:59,710 --> 00:24:00,400
Well...

387
00:24:00,880 --> 00:24:03,570
just having them pick you up
and drop you off when I'm not around.

388
00:24:03,590 --> 00:24:04,680
And...

389
00:24:05,570 --> 00:24:07,010
keeping an eye on you
outside the condo.

390
00:24:07,280 --> 00:24:08,190
That's all.

391
00:24:10,250 --> 00:24:11,330
That's all, huh?

392
00:24:38,240 --> 00:24:39,170
What are you doing?

393
00:24:41,540 --> 00:24:42,560
What?

394
00:24:44,350 --> 00:24:45,410
What's that mark on your neck?

395
00:24:47,400 --> 00:24:49,450
Oh, it's just a scratch.

396
00:24:52,270 --> 00:24:54,400
Aw, what kind of mark is that, really?

397
00:24:55,480 --> 00:24:56,920
Just stick to your game.

398
00:24:56,950 --> 00:24:58,140
I'm watching YouTube.

399
00:24:59,780 --> 00:25:01,250
Yeah, just keep watching then.

400
00:25:07,540 --> 00:25:09,400
When can we go to the beach again?

401
00:25:09,430 --> 00:25:10,140
Right?

402
00:25:10,450 --> 00:25:12,100
But this time,
I'm not going in the summer.

403
00:25:12,200 --> 00:25:13,610
Which season? How about "lovely"?

404
00:25:24,110 --> 00:25:25,320
Heading back together?

405
00:25:27,920 --> 00:25:32,120
Look at you being all tiny.
Acting like you're only 3 cm tall, bud.

406
00:25:32,150 --> 00:25:34,030
Yeah. Look at you. All shy, huh?

407
00:25:36,860 --> 00:25:38,200
What are you laughing at?

408
00:25:39,250 --> 00:25:41,010
I didn't.

409
00:25:42,430 --> 00:25:43,540
Stop laughing.

410
00:25:44,030 --> 00:25:44,950
What are you talking about?

411
00:25:45,130 --> 00:25:46,750
Well, you were just laughing.

412
00:25:47,070 --> 00:25:48,410
No, I wasn't, baby.

413
00:25:49,990 --> 00:25:50,900
What's with the "baby"?

414
00:25:52,310 --> 00:25:53,470
"No, I wasn't, baby."

415
00:25:53,810 --> 00:25:55,120
This one too.

416
00:25:55,140 --> 00:25:57,180
His voice usually doesn't sound like this.

417
00:25:57,650 --> 00:26:00,500
Now my friend's voice
is all cutesy and high-pitched.

418
00:26:00,530 --> 00:26:03,010
Ugh, I'm sick of this lovey-dovey stuff.

419
00:26:03,430 --> 00:26:05,140
When are you guys going public?

420
00:26:08,580 --> 00:26:09,700
Fine, how about now?

421
00:26:19,250 --> 00:26:20,780
The two of us...

422
00:26:24,210 --> 00:26:25,170
are dating.

423
00:26:29,400 --> 00:26:30,550
Are we?

424
00:26:32,960 --> 00:26:34,730
- Quick, answer!
- Yeah, we are.

425
00:26:35,260 --> 00:26:36,010
Hey!

426
00:26:36,560 --> 00:26:37,900
What did Podduang say, Tod?

427
00:26:37,980 --> 00:26:40,250
I didn't really hear it, man.

428
00:26:40,430 --> 00:26:41,880
- Quick, answer!
- Uh, I don't know.

429
00:26:41,910 --> 00:26:42,880
I don't know what he said.

430
00:26:42,900 --> 00:26:45,330
- Mumble, mumble.
- Come on, what was it?

431
00:26:45,350 --> 00:26:46,750
- Come on, say it.
- Hurry up!

432
00:26:46,770 --> 00:26:48,040
- What should I say?
- Just say it! Speak up!

433
00:26:48,070 --> 00:26:48,970
- Say it again, quick!
- Huh?

434
00:26:48,990 --> 00:26:50,310
- Say it again! Come on!
- Tell us!

435
00:26:52,300 --> 00:26:53,480
Come on, let's hear it.

436
00:26:53,500 --> 00:26:55,410
- Hurry!
- Podduang, say it!

437
00:26:55,870 --> 00:26:57,280
I'm waiting to hear it, hurry!

438
00:26:59,410 --> 00:27:00,180
Alright!

439
00:27:01,430 --> 00:27:02,790
Jin and I are dating!

440
00:27:04,970 --> 00:27:05,980
Is that clear enough?

441
00:27:06,010 --> 00:27:07,940
- Oh.
- I see.

442
00:27:07,960 --> 00:27:10,430
- Crystal clear.
- Loud and clear.

443
00:27:10,460 --> 00:27:14,020
♫I don't need a reason, as long as you're mine♫

444
00:27:14,790 --> 00:27:16,630
♫As long as you hold my hand♫

445
00:27:16,650 --> 00:27:18,040
Hey, everyone.

446
00:27:18,060 --> 00:27:19,830
Was that clear?

447
00:27:19,850 --> 00:27:22,560
- Loud and clear.
- We heard you.

448
00:27:23,380 --> 00:27:25,650
- I can't stay here anymore.
- Where are you going?

449
00:27:25,670 --> 00:27:27,100
Grab him!

450
00:27:27,370 --> 00:27:29,240
Yeah, good, hold him tight.

451
00:27:29,950 --> 00:27:30,880
Go ahead.

452
00:27:30,910 --> 00:27:32,020
- My bag!
- He's totally blushing.

453
00:27:32,040 --> 00:27:33,140
What?

454
00:27:33,500 --> 00:27:34,860
- I'm going home.
- Give me the bag.

455
00:27:34,890 --> 00:27:35,730
Yes, baby.

456
00:27:35,750 --> 00:27:36,580
Right, baby.

457
00:27:37,230 --> 00:27:38,250
- Yes, baby.
- Bye-bye.

458
00:27:38,280 --> 00:27:40,100
- Bye-bye.
- See you, baby.

459
00:27:47,280 --> 00:27:51,280
[Jinna: I'm going to my dad's condo today
to check more CCTV footage.]

460
00:27:54,590 --> 00:27:56,800
[Podduang: Okay. Stop by when you're done.]

461
00:28:31,980 --> 00:28:33,260
Can I come in?

462
00:28:36,700 --> 00:28:37,580
Yes.

463
00:28:54,760 --> 00:28:55,740
Thank you.

464
00:29:05,450 --> 00:29:06,540
So...

465
00:29:08,380 --> 00:29:10,310
it really wasn't you
who killed Anda, right?

466
00:29:13,480 --> 00:29:15,210
Why would I do that?

467
00:29:18,970 --> 00:29:19,700
And...

468
00:29:20,730 --> 00:29:22,500
why did you run away?

469
00:29:26,720 --> 00:29:27,980
The reason I came here

470
00:29:29,350 --> 00:29:31,780
is because I wanted to
tell you the whole truth.

471
00:29:32,770 --> 00:29:34,190
If you didn't do anything wrong,

472
00:29:34,760 --> 00:29:36,210
why are you so afraid?

473
00:29:42,940 --> 00:29:44,200
Because I know

474
00:29:44,520 --> 00:29:45,630
that if I stayed...

475
00:29:46,870 --> 00:29:48,330
I'd be dead for sure.

476
00:29:52,010 --> 00:29:53,360
What do you mean by that?

477
00:29:57,540 --> 00:29:59,210
Then promise me.

478
00:30:01,470 --> 00:30:03,020
Don't tell anyone about this.

479
00:30:04,170 --> 00:30:06,520
And I won't get involved
in this matter ever again.

480
00:30:09,750 --> 00:30:10,660
Then...

481
00:30:11,860 --> 00:30:13,340
let me ask you one more thing.

482
00:30:17,340 --> 00:30:19,380
Did you send me the threatening message?

483
00:30:22,780 --> 00:30:23,920
What message?

484
00:30:27,580 --> 00:30:29,970
[Don't get involved in Anda's case
if you still wanna live.]

485
00:30:32,370 --> 00:30:34,030
It's a death threat.

486
00:30:36,240 --> 00:30:39,510
The son of Tycoon Chanin,
Mr. Jinna Ronnarak,

487
00:30:39,530 --> 00:30:42,770
who is currently an undergraduate student,

488
00:30:42,800 --> 00:30:47,110
- has now taken over the business...
- Is Jin's dad really this rich?

489
00:30:47,140 --> 00:30:49,270
- An official press conference was held.
- Why?

490
00:30:49,430 --> 00:30:51,660
Do you want your parents
to come and say,

491
00:30:51,850 --> 00:30:53,350
"Actually,

492
00:30:53,450 --> 00:30:54,970
our family is worth millions, son"?

493
00:30:54,990 --> 00:30:56,730
Well, wouldn't that be nice?

494
00:30:57,000 --> 00:30:59,160
So I could take care of you comfortably.

495
00:30:59,590 --> 00:31:00,880
Look who's talking.

496
00:31:05,370 --> 00:31:06,010
Dunk.

497
00:31:07,060 --> 00:31:08,420
Do rich guys

498
00:31:09,150 --> 00:31:10,550
change cars often?

499
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:16,210
Doesn't it depend
on how rich they are?

500
00:31:16,890 --> 00:31:18,880
James changes cars very often.

501
00:31:19,370 --> 00:31:20,940
But lately, there's nothing.

502
00:31:20,960 --> 00:31:22,310
Has he sold them all just to survive?

503
00:31:22,330 --> 00:31:24,520
He has no work,
and his personality is trash.

504
00:31:24,640 --> 00:31:25,400
Yeah.

505
00:31:25,710 --> 00:31:27,230
He's a gambling addict, too.

506
00:31:28,910 --> 00:31:30,810
Wait, how do you know this?

507
00:31:31,850 --> 00:31:33,670
Just look at him.
You don't even need to dig deep.

508
00:31:33,860 --> 00:31:35,180
Those people who flaunt their money

509
00:31:35,210 --> 00:31:38,540
are almost always into
online gambling and slot machines.

510
00:31:42,270 --> 00:31:44,580
[Audio, AC, Window Tint,]

511
00:31:44,610 --> 00:31:46,310
[Anti-theft, Car Accessories]

512
00:31:46,330 --> 00:31:48,710
I'm sure it's here.

513
00:31:48,740 --> 00:31:49,810
I think so, too.

514
00:31:49,840 --> 00:31:51,080
It's the last place.

515
00:32:00,590 --> 00:32:01,460
Hello?

516
00:32:01,590 --> 00:32:02,430
Hello, Jin.

517
00:32:02,840 --> 00:32:03,880
What are you doing?

518
00:32:04,050 --> 00:32:05,920
Checking the CCTV footage. What's up?

519
00:32:06,270 --> 00:32:09,510
I found the garage
where Anda got his car fixed.

520
00:32:09,540 --> 00:32:10,730
But it's weird.

521
00:32:10,750 --> 00:32:14,000
Does Itti really not know that
Anda brought the car here?

522
00:32:14,030 --> 00:32:15,650
His relative owns the place.

523
00:32:16,170 --> 00:32:18,340
I don't know. That's what he said.

524
00:32:18,700 --> 00:32:19,620
Yeah, yeah.

525
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:21,630
I'll go in and talk to them first.

526
00:32:22,550 --> 00:32:23,890
Mm, okay.

527
00:32:28,180 --> 00:32:29,250
What's next?

528
00:32:30,110 --> 00:32:31,620
Let's go. What are we waiting for?

529
00:32:31,660 --> 00:32:33,030
Oh, Mr. Jin.

530
00:32:33,050 --> 00:32:35,800
I found something in this footage.

531
00:32:36,380 --> 00:32:37,320
What is it?

532
00:32:38,130 --> 00:32:40,330
That security guard
who stole the stuff

533
00:32:40,360 --> 00:32:42,590
was seen with this person.

534
00:32:43,420 --> 00:32:45,370
That's one of Itti's men.

535
00:32:48,260 --> 00:32:49,740
Could you zoom in for me?

536
00:32:49,760 --> 00:32:50,580
Yes, I can.

537
00:32:57,390 --> 00:33:00,180
How nice of him.
He's even giving money away.

538
00:33:13,060 --> 00:33:14,110
I admit it.

539
00:33:14,660 --> 00:33:16,800
I was an Anda hater.

540
00:33:17,280 --> 00:33:19,400
Back then, I hated Anda so much that...

541
00:33:20,620 --> 00:33:22,380
I couldn't see anything clearly.

542
00:33:23,850 --> 00:33:26,780
I stalked Anda until I knew everything.

543
00:33:27,290 --> 00:33:31,200
I learned that
Anda was actually a very lovely kid.

544
00:33:34,080 --> 00:33:35,720
Unlike his brother.

545
00:33:39,190 --> 00:33:40,640
You mean...

546
00:33:41,270 --> 00:33:42,470
Itti?

547
00:33:42,810 --> 00:33:43,780
He's the one.

548
00:33:44,300 --> 00:33:46,590
The person I think killed Anda.

549
00:33:52,330 --> 00:33:53,290
Hello.

550
00:33:53,730 --> 00:33:55,890
How can I help you?

551
00:33:57,800 --> 00:34:01,950
We're investigating Anda's case together.

552
00:34:02,120 --> 00:34:04,720
You should know him, right?

553
00:34:04,950 --> 00:34:07,190
Well, Anda...

554
00:34:07,470 --> 00:34:10,020
was a close friend of ours.

555
00:34:10,050 --> 00:34:13,159
But you see, after Anda passed away,

556
00:34:13,179 --> 00:34:17,010
there's reason to believe he was murdered.

557
00:34:21,960 --> 00:34:26,010
So, could we get some information

558
00:34:26,070 --> 00:34:27,630
about when Anda brought his car in?

559
00:34:27,650 --> 00:34:28,690
No, you can't.

560
00:34:31,320 --> 00:34:32,409
Look, sir.

561
00:34:32,830 --> 00:34:35,100
We don't need the information, but...

562
00:34:35,310 --> 00:34:36,219
can we see the CCTV footage?

563
00:34:36,239 --> 00:34:38,330
It's an invasion of privacy.

564
00:34:39,090 --> 00:34:42,360
Hey, but if they don't know,

565
00:34:43,040 --> 00:34:44,880
it wouldn't be an invasion, right?

566
00:34:45,370 --> 00:34:46,600
Come on.

567
00:34:55,870 --> 00:34:57,200
Alright, how about this?

568
00:34:57,930 --> 00:34:58,860
A thousand.

569
00:35:02,720 --> 00:35:03,930
How about two thousand?

570
00:35:04,510 --> 00:35:05,440
Art!

571
00:35:07,750 --> 00:35:08,800
Then...

572
00:35:09,350 --> 00:35:11,760
Three thousand. That's my final offer.

573
00:35:18,210 --> 00:35:20,560
Anek, come to the counter, please.

574
00:35:27,330 --> 00:35:28,390
That's enough, you guys.

575
00:35:28,730 --> 00:35:30,270
I don't have time for games.

576
00:35:30,560 --> 00:35:31,940
Please take care of them for me.

577
00:35:31,960 --> 00:35:33,420
If they bother us again,

578
00:35:33,730 --> 00:35:34,810
you can handle them.

579
00:35:37,680 --> 00:35:39,240
You two heard him.

580
00:35:39,670 --> 00:35:41,860
Don't cause any more trouble. Go!

581
00:35:43,310 --> 00:35:45,400
Don't come here ever again.

582
00:35:48,960 --> 00:35:49,910
Are you alright?

583
00:35:51,130 --> 00:35:53,810
How was that?
Solving problems with money.

584
00:35:55,880 --> 00:35:57,180
Dammit.

585
00:35:57,540 --> 00:35:58,930
I really thought he'd take it.

586
00:36:05,080 --> 00:36:06,100
Yes, Mr. Jin.

587
00:36:06,560 --> 00:36:08,000
Podduang isn't answering my calls.

588
00:36:08,240 --> 00:36:09,890
Can you check on him?

589
00:36:10,190 --> 00:36:11,110
Will do.

590
00:36:11,590 --> 00:36:13,230
Keep me posted on what happens.

591
00:36:15,130 --> 00:36:16,000
Why...

592
00:36:16,770 --> 00:36:19,820
do you think Itti killed
his own brother?

593
00:36:24,510 --> 00:36:26,420
I think I know too much.

594
00:36:29,770 --> 00:36:30,690
Wow.

595
00:36:31,230 --> 00:36:32,540
I used to go to
the gambling den with James.

596
00:36:32,570 --> 00:36:33,630
The smell of money sure is sweet.

597
00:36:33,650 --> 00:36:35,410
James was famous back then.

598
00:36:35,730 --> 00:36:37,390
What are we doing here?

599
00:36:38,710 --> 00:36:40,250
Getting you some spending money.

600
00:36:40,270 --> 00:36:41,860
Hey, no need to cling to me.

601
00:36:45,450 --> 00:36:47,190
Itti was there, too.

602
00:36:48,830 --> 00:36:49,680
There he is.

603
00:36:50,590 --> 00:36:51,420
He's here.

604
00:36:53,050 --> 00:36:54,520
Greet him.

605
00:36:55,090 --> 00:36:55,770
What's up, James?

606
00:36:55,790 --> 00:36:57,190
- Hello.
- Hello.

607
00:36:57,910 --> 00:36:59,190
Ready to get rich today?

608
00:36:59,340 --> 00:37:00,410
Ready as always.

609
00:37:00,650 --> 00:37:01,650
Go on, go for it.

610
00:37:03,190 --> 00:37:04,480
I've been on a lucky streak lately.

611
00:37:04,680 --> 00:37:05,270
Go.

612
00:37:06,190 --> 00:37:06,810
Quickly.

613
00:37:07,240 --> 00:37:08,210
How much will you bet?

614
00:37:08,330 --> 00:37:09,600
Please, come in.

615
00:37:09,770 --> 00:37:10,860
What's the limit?

616
00:37:10,890 --> 00:37:12,300
- No limit.
- This was also where James...

617
00:37:12,330 --> 00:37:13,390
- liked to trade cars.
- Hello, boss.

618
00:37:14,620 --> 00:37:17,500
And it seemed to be involved
in other illegal businesses.

619
00:37:19,190 --> 00:37:21,090
Thank you for every bit of support...

620
00:37:21,110 --> 00:37:22,750
that was sent to both of us.

621
00:37:22,780 --> 00:37:24,080
You've acted in three series now.

622
00:37:24,110 --> 00:37:25,980
When will you become a real couple?

623
00:37:26,000 --> 00:37:28,830
And when James started
working on series with Anda,

624
00:37:28,860 --> 00:37:31,540
- he became famous and made more money.
- When should it be?

625
00:37:31,560 --> 00:37:33,620
Then James started to change.

626
00:37:34,510 --> 00:37:37,970
That's when I started to hate Anda to the core.

627
00:37:38,320 --> 00:37:42,120
So I created a hater account to attack him.

628
00:37:43,470 --> 00:37:46,800
I started digging up stories
about Anda's family to post.

629
00:37:47,180 --> 00:37:49,410
Until I found out that Itti

630
00:37:49,870 --> 00:37:52,400
was actually the owner
of the gambling den

631
00:37:52,430 --> 00:37:53,970
and those illegal businesses.

632
00:37:53,990 --> 00:37:54,600
[Pol. Lt. Col. Itti Thamprateep]

633
00:37:54,630 --> 00:37:56,610
The more money James made,
[Has Officially Assumed the Position.]

634
00:37:56,630 --> 00:37:59,860
the more debt he owed to Itti's gambling den.

635
00:38:02,250 --> 00:38:04,860
Stop messing with Anda already.

636
00:38:04,880 --> 00:38:06,690
You know he's our cash cow.

637
00:38:08,910 --> 00:38:11,020
I know you like him.

638
00:38:13,630 --> 00:38:15,360
Like him? What the hell is wrong with you?

639
00:38:15,630 --> 00:38:16,950
Are you insane?

640
00:38:17,950 --> 00:38:19,180
If I don't do it,

641
00:38:19,440 --> 00:38:20,510
we don't get the money.

642
00:38:21,150 --> 00:38:22,120
And do you have any?

643
00:38:22,290 --> 00:38:23,880
Give it to me then.
Five hundred thousand.

644
00:38:24,770 --> 00:38:27,610
Haven't I been taking care of you all this time?

645
00:38:27,950 --> 00:38:29,370
You're so annoying.

646
00:38:54,250 --> 00:38:55,410
I know everything.

647
00:38:57,650 --> 00:38:59,090
You should leave him.

648
00:39:02,730 --> 00:39:05,230
That day changed the way I saw Anda.

649
00:39:06,160 --> 00:39:09,780
So I decided to tell him
everything about his brother.

650
00:39:11,280 --> 00:39:12,340
Are you okay?

651
00:39:12,560 --> 00:39:13,700
Can you get up?

652
00:39:14,600 --> 00:39:15,510
Take it slow.

653
00:39:23,040 --> 00:39:26,710
And all the evidence I had against Itti...

654
00:39:28,540 --> 00:39:30,130
I gave it all to Anda.

655
00:39:33,130 --> 00:39:34,420
That evidence...

656
00:39:36,030 --> 00:39:37,110
What did it consist of?

657
00:39:41,180 --> 00:39:42,130
[Standard Installation and Maintenance Services]

658
00:39:42,150 --> 00:39:43,260
[Anti-theft Alarms,
Windows, Central Locking Systems]

659
00:39:43,290 --> 00:39:44,460
Dammit.

660
00:39:44,780 --> 00:39:46,280
What a total waste of time.

661
00:39:48,660 --> 00:39:50,200
Why do we

662
00:39:51,210 --> 00:39:53,860
have to sit on the side of the road
like a couple of sad pups?

663
00:39:59,810 --> 00:40:00,900
Do you think

664
00:40:01,930 --> 00:40:04,280
we'll ever find Anda's killer?

665
00:40:06,230 --> 00:40:08,150
Everyone is giving it their all.

666
00:40:08,420 --> 00:40:09,780
I'm sure we'll find them.

667
00:40:12,290 --> 00:40:13,020
Yeah.

668
00:40:14,530 --> 00:40:16,270
I feel so damn sorry for Anda.

669
00:40:40,630 --> 00:40:42,670
[Castrol Oil Change Service Center]

670
00:40:43,460 --> 00:40:44,030
Hey.

671
00:40:47,530 --> 00:40:49,000
Are you thinking what I'm thinking?

672
00:40:49,690 --> 00:40:51,020
Exactly what you're thinking.

673
00:41:08,140 --> 00:41:09,230
What are you guys doing?

674
00:41:10,390 --> 00:41:11,180
Investigating something?

675
00:41:13,340 --> 00:41:13,960
Hey!

676
00:41:14,400 --> 00:41:16,730
You already got a thousand.
Stop talking.

677
00:41:17,120 --> 00:41:18,450
Tell me.

678
00:41:18,470 --> 00:41:19,730
I want to know.

679
00:41:21,230 --> 00:41:22,350
A murderer?

680
00:41:36,250 --> 00:41:37,350
Hey, there he is, Tod.

681
00:41:50,840 --> 00:41:51,690
Shit.

682
00:41:52,550 --> 00:41:53,700
Itti?

683
00:41:54,990 --> 00:41:56,380
Shit, it's Itti.

684
00:41:58,790 --> 00:42:00,070
By the way...

685
00:42:01,540 --> 00:42:02,570
Who is this Itti anyway?

686
00:42:02,990 --> 00:42:04,310
Just get lost.

687
00:42:09,270 --> 00:42:10,410
Is anyone here?

688
00:42:10,440 --> 00:42:11,390
Yes?

689
00:42:12,990 --> 00:42:14,100
Oh, it's you.

690
00:42:14,470 --> 00:42:15,530
Is your dad here?

691
00:42:17,010 --> 00:42:18,910
No, he hasn't been home for two days.

692
00:42:18,930 --> 00:42:20,530
Do you know where he went?

693
00:42:21,300 --> 00:42:22,270
I don't know.

694
00:42:23,100 --> 00:42:24,370
Let me ask you something.

695
00:42:24,400 --> 00:42:26,220
When your dad took those stolen things,

696
00:42:27,060 --> 00:42:28,730
did he talk to anyone else back then?

697
00:42:30,280 --> 00:42:31,840
Just you guys.

698
00:42:33,660 --> 00:42:34,770
Oh.

699
00:42:34,800 --> 00:42:38,600
The other day, I heard him talking
on the phone with someone.

700
00:42:38,690 --> 00:42:40,510
It sounded like he was asking for money.

701
00:42:40,530 --> 00:42:41,930
Did you hear anything else?

702
00:42:43,090 --> 00:42:46,800
I heard something
about keeping secrets to expose someone.

703
00:42:46,830 --> 00:42:50,320
Something about a phone and a laptop.

704
00:42:54,260 --> 00:42:55,640
Did he happen to mention any names?

705
00:42:57,070 --> 00:42:58,350
And do you know...

706
00:42:59,070 --> 00:43:01,360
that Itti once threatened to kill James

707
00:43:01,380 --> 00:43:02,720
over a debt?

708
00:43:03,030 --> 00:43:05,200
Itti is just that terrible.

709
00:43:12,790 --> 00:43:14,100
[Where are you?
Let's meet up. I'm worried.]

710
00:43:14,130 --> 00:43:15,380
[I've paid off all my debts now.
Let's run away together.]

711
00:43:15,400 --> 00:43:16,370
[Let's start a new life together,
the three of us.]

712
00:43:21,450 --> 00:43:22,710
Is something wrong?

713
00:43:24,310 --> 00:43:25,480
Nothing.

714
00:43:26,330 --> 00:43:27,790
I think I...

715
00:43:28,960 --> 00:43:30,190
I should go now.

716
00:43:31,460 --> 00:43:34,180
You take care of yourself, too.

717
00:43:35,710 --> 00:43:36,440
Okay.

718
00:43:41,910 --> 00:43:44,750
I hope what I've told you
can help you and your friends.

719
00:43:58,200 --> 00:43:59,410
Uh, Amp.

720
00:44:02,280 --> 00:44:04,000
Please leave through
the back of the condo.

721
00:44:04,510 --> 00:44:06,120
The front is quite dangerous.

722
00:44:51,160 --> 00:44:52,000
Jin.

723
00:44:54,460 --> 00:44:55,390
Podduang.

724
00:44:59,010 --> 00:44:59,810
Jin.

725
00:45:02,420 --> 00:45:03,400
Podduang.

726
00:45:06,070 --> 00:45:08,220
Jin, go help Podduang!

727
00:45:09,600 --> 00:45:10,900
Go help Podduang!

728
00:45:29,940 --> 00:45:31,220
How are you doing?

729
00:45:31,990 --> 00:45:33,190
I'm scared.

730
00:45:33,290 --> 00:45:35,280
So I didn't dare go anywhere.

731
00:45:38,130 --> 00:45:41,440
Then why did you decide to come out so easily?

732
00:45:49,150 --> 00:45:49,810
But...

733
00:45:50,700 --> 00:45:51,250
Hey!

734
00:45:55,150 --> 00:45:55,850
Hey!

735
00:45:56,460 --> 00:45:57,310
What are you doing?

736
00:46:04,470 --> 00:46:05,600
You guys...

737
00:46:06,220 --> 00:46:07,950
really have a death wish.

738
00:46:19,320 --> 00:46:20,980
Almost everyone is here, I see.

739
00:46:22,210 --> 00:46:23,200
Who's missing?

740
00:46:25,170 --> 00:46:26,560
Oh.

741
00:46:26,770 --> 00:46:28,010
Jin, right?

742
00:46:29,950 --> 00:46:30,710
Jin.

743
00:46:31,130 --> 00:46:32,270
Go help Podduang.

744
00:46:32,590 --> 00:46:33,220
Go.

745
00:46:33,250 --> 00:46:34,140
Jin.

746
00:46:34,370 --> 00:46:35,610
Go help Podduang!

747
00:46:36,130 --> 00:46:37,810
How could you do this, Itti?

748
00:46:40,620 --> 00:46:41,930
Now, why don't you tell me...

749
00:46:42,190 --> 00:46:43,500
out of these three,

750
00:46:44,040 --> 00:46:45,690
who is the least connected to the others?

751
00:46:45,910 --> 00:46:47,200
I don't know this guy.

752
00:46:48,750 --> 00:46:49,860
And as for Amp,

753
00:46:49,890 --> 00:46:51,620
I don't give a shit about her anymore.

754
00:46:55,040 --> 00:46:56,080
Good.

755
00:46:56,780 --> 00:46:58,400
Your job is done, then.

756
00:47:00,350 --> 00:47:01,490
As promised,

757
00:47:02,610 --> 00:47:04,030
your debt is cleared.

758
00:47:05,860 --> 00:47:06,800
Which means...

759
00:47:10,820 --> 00:47:12,280
you're useless now.

760
00:47:32,330 --> 00:47:34,220
Now, who's next?

761
00:47:42,070 --> 00:47:43,370
What the hell do you want?

762
00:47:43,600 --> 00:47:44,580
Just say it!

763
00:47:44,600 --> 00:47:46,450
Everything you've got on me.

764
00:47:46,470 --> 00:47:47,200
I want it all.

765
00:47:47,230 --> 00:47:50,110
What makes you think
I'd wanna keep your dirty little secrets?

766
00:47:50,130 --> 00:47:51,200
What are you looking for, Mr. Jin?

767
00:47:51,230 --> 00:47:54,120
Anything that can store data.

768
00:47:54,140 --> 00:47:56,460
This isn't the kind of person
Dad raised you to be.

769
00:47:56,490 --> 00:47:58,700
This is all your fault.

770
00:47:59,430 --> 00:48:00,520
You did this.

771
00:48:00,710 --> 00:48:01,880
You and only you.

772
00:48:01,900 --> 00:48:04,490
I think Itti might have abducted Podduang.

773
00:48:04,640 --> 00:48:05,980
No matter how many people you kill,

774
00:48:06,010 --> 00:48:07,590
your life will never get better.

775
00:48:07,610 --> 00:48:09,940
I'm not the one who's supposed to die tonight.

776
00:48:09,970 --> 00:48:11,500
You are.

